Importer: a ProgressHandler whose Update() answers false cancels the import

Jahshaka's own change (not upstream), STAGE-CLOSE-TRIAGE-1 round 5.

The bug
-------
ProgressHandler::Update() documents "return false to abort loading at the next
possible occasion (loaders and Assimp are generally allowed to perform all
needed cleanup tasks prior to returning control to the caller)", but nothing in
the pinned tree reads its return: Importer::ReadFile calls the void
UpdateFileRead() and ApplyPostProcessing the void UpdatePostProcess(), which
discard Update()'s answer. A bake cancelled at quit (MeshBake's progress
handler) therefore waited out the whole parse and every post-processing step;
past the app's 20 s shutdown bound that is a forced exit.

The fix
-------
Two cancel points honouring the documented contract:
  * ReadFile, once the format's read returned a scene, before any
    post-processing;
  * ApplyPostProcessing, before each post-processing step.
On a false answer the partial scene is freed, the import returns nullptr and
GetErrorString() names the cancel. A handler that never answers false (the
default one) changes nothing: one extra Update(-1) call per step.

diff --git a/code/Common/Importer.cpp b/code/Common/Importer.cpp
index 684419b94..b82e81ce3 100644
